         TITLE 'RAKFPWH - Salted password hash (SHA-256 of SALT||PW)'
RAKFPWH  CSECT
         PRINT NOGEN
*
**********************************************************************
*                                                                    *
* NAME: RAKFPWH                                                      *
*                                                                    *
* TYPE: Assembler Source - reentrant callable subroutine            *
*                                                                    *
* DESC: Compute the RAKF salted password hash.  This is the SINGLE   *
*       definition of the hashing convention:                        *
*                                                                    *
*           digest = SHA-256( SALT(8 bytes) || PASSWORD(pwlen) )     *
*                                                                    *
*       Login verification (ICHSFR00) and password enrollment (the   *
*       cc370 ADDUSER/ALTUSER tools) MUST both call this routine so  *
*       they agree byte-for-byte.  Verify = call RAKFPWH, then CLC   *
*       the 32-byte result against the stored hash.  Set = generate  *
*       an 8-byte salt (STCK), call RAKFPWH, store salt+result.      *
*                                                                    *
*       Password bytes are hashed exactly as supplied (EBCDIC on     *
*       MVS) - set and verify run on the same system, so the code    *
*       page is consistent.                                          *
*                                                                    *
*       Pure computation - issues NO SVCs, fully reentrant, so it    *
*       is callable from ICHSFR00's key-0 login path and from        *
*       problem-state tooling alike.  Calls RAKFHASH (link both).    *
*                                                                    *
* LINKAGE: Standard OS.  R1 -> parameter list of 5 addresses:        *
*                                                                    *
*   PLIST+0   A(SALT)     8-byte salt                               *
*   PLIST+4   A(PASSWORD) password bytes                            *
*   PLIST+8   A(PWLEN)    fullword password length (1..8)           *
*   PLIST+12  A(OUTPUT)   32-byte area for the raw digest           *
*   PLIST+16  A(WORK)     work area, >= RPWWORKL bytes              *
*                                                                    *
*   R13 -> caller's 18-word save area.                              *
*                                                                    *
* RETURN: R15 = 0 (RAKFHASH cannot fail for these <=16-byte inputs)  *
*                                                                    *
**********************************************************************
         SPACE 1
         SAVE  (14,12)            save caller's regs in HIS area
         LR    R12,R15            program base
         USING RAKFPWH,R12
         LR    R9,R1              keep parameter-list pointer
         L     R11,16(,R9)        R11 -> caller work area
         USING RPWWORKD,R11
*
* --- chain our own save area (we call out to RAKFHASH) ----------- *
*
         LA    R2,RPWSAVE
         ST    R13,4(,R2)         back chain -> caller save area
         ST    R2,8(,R13)         forward chain
         LR    R13,R2             R13 -> our save area
         SPACE 1
*
* --- build SALT(8) || PASSWORD(pwlen) in PWBUF ------------------- *
*
         L     R3,0(,R9)          A(salt)
         MVC   PWBUF(8),0(R3)     salt into first 8 bytes
         L     R4,8(,R9)          A(pwlen)
         L     R4,0(,R4)          pwlen value
         L     R5,4(,R9)          A(password)
         LR    R6,R4              pwlen
         BCTR  R6,0               pwlen-1 for EX
         EX    R6,PWMVC           MVC PWBUF+8(pwlen),0(R5)
         LA    R6,8               hash length = 8 + pwlen
         AR    R6,R4
         ST    R6,PWHLEN
         SPACE 1
*
* --- call RAKFHASH(A(PWBUF),A(PWHLEN),A(OUTPUT),A(PWHWK)) --------- *
*
         LA    R0,PWBUF
         ST    R0,RPWPL+0
         LA    R0,PWHLEN
         ST    R0,RPWPL+4
         L     R0,12(,R9)         caller's A(OUTPUT)
         ST    R0,RPWPL+8
         LA    R0,PWHWK
         ST    R0,RPWPL+12
         LA    R1,RPWPL
         L     R15,=V(RAKFHASH)
         BALR  R14,R15
         SPACE 1
*
* --- return ------------------------------------------------------ *
*
         L     R13,4(,R13)        restore caller save area
         RETURN (14,12),RC=0
         SPACE 2
*
* --- Executed MVC (length filled in by EX) ----------------------- *
*
PWMVC    MVC   PWBUF+8(0),0(R5)
         SPACE 1
         LTORG
         SPACE 2
**********************************************************************
* Caller-provided work area (mapped, not allocated here)           *
**********************************************************************
RPWWORKD DSECT
RPWSAVE  DS    18F                save area for calling RAKFHASH
RPWPL    DS    4F                 parameter list to RAKFHASH
PWBUF    DS    CL16               SALT(8) || PASSWORD(<=8)
PWHLEN   DS    F                  hash input length (8+pwlen)
PWHWK    DS    CL512              RAKFHASH work area (>= RHWORKL)
RPWWORKL EQU   *-RPWWORKD         required work-area size
         SPACE 1
         YREGS
         END   RAKFPWH
